{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team","id":1524568,"title":"Cross-over team","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-26T20:27:07-07:00","id":1524568,"title":"Cross-over team","content":"Here's the question, there's a team of seven people, eight with ST, who want to play a cross-over, but would like a second opinion on how to do it. The points I would like you to focus on are the following:<br /> <br /> How to fit different creatures into the same team? They intend to play characters from multiple games, so a hint as to what goal/circumstance would bring them together would be welcome. Exclude hunter, these are just antagonists in this chronicle.<br /> <br /> What beings should be included? All games have antagonists, but I wanted opinions on which ones to use, because obviously it won't be possible to use everything and it would be good not to include a group that wouldn't exactly be a threat, it would also be good to know to what extent these threats could cooperate with each other.<br /> <br /> In the case of a chronicle within a large city, which groups do you believe should be included in the formation of that city? I know they intend to use Vampires and Werewolves (and maybe beasts), but some other working examples would be good too, just to not get too generic or messy.<br /> <br /> Basically that's it, and to make it clear, I'm not participating in the chronicle so there are things that I don't know how to explain why they are like that, maybe they just thought it is cool.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T00:54:13-07:00","id":1524575,"title":"","content":"That is very broad.<br /> <br /> For antagonists, I would suggest one of the major one's, like the God-machine, or the Exarchs, or the Judges, or maybe even a Conspiracy from Deviant, something which is a large threat.<br /> <br /> Possibly two of these (one as a potential ally and future antagonists) or if you want deeper politics, use a least three more minor factions (not antagonists, but like the Lancea, Guardians of the Veil and Storm Lords all trying to get the players to side with them over a number of resources/events/missions).<br /> <br /> So everyone is either focussed on one big undefeatable evil (which can be undermined in some way, but ultimately it is a very big threat to everyone) or everyone is approached by a powerful (but not cosmically so) group which they can choose to work for or against (or you can do both).<br /> <br /> Including vampires can be more difficult, unless they can work through ghouled proxies during the day, or something similar. But that is something to discuss with the vampire players. Including a Mummy can be very messy given their unusual relationship with time.<br /> <br /> Lastly 7 players is a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T04:37:06-07:00","id":1524583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524575#post1524575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is very broad.<br /> <br /> ...Lastly 7 players is a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know and the guy already did with 9 players so... I just accept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T07:05:41-07:00","id":1524586,"title":"","content":"Are all those players going to play the \u2018main\u2019 splats, over the \u2018dyad\u2019 splats? (As in, Uratha over Wolf-Blooded, or Kindred over ghouls) Because the more main splats you mix, the harder it will be for bookkeeping\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> For non-Hunter teams, them all being part of a werewolf pack or a Bound krewe seems easiest. Or some custom-made Mystery Cult they all follow.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they all used to be part of an exteded family as mortals, who all got turned into/ secretly were all along separate types of supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T08:14:37-07:00","id":1524587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524586#post1524586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are all those players going to play the \u2018main\u2019 splats, over the \u2018dyad\u2019 splats? (As in, Uratha over Wolf-Blooded, or Kindred over ghouls) Because the more main splats you mix, the harder it will be for bookkeeping\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> For non-Hunter teams, them all being part of a werewolf pack or a Bound krewe seems easiest. Or some custom-made Mystery Cult they all follow.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they all used to be part of an exteded family as mortals, who all got turned into/ secretly were all along separate types of supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, but I think there is at least one of them who prefers to play dhampir or vampire, or play as a hero. Send a suggestion and I'll discuss it with them. The part about being a family seems good to me, but it limits it a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T08:56:16-07:00","id":1524589,"title":"","content":"What to include or exclude is an interesting question. One of the answers to that will depend upon how big of a gap in power are you comfortable with and how much stepping on toes is okay. Mummies are much stronger than pretty much everything except experienced Mages, on the bottom end you have mortals (including hunters, not including mages). Deviants can fall virtually anywhere on the power chart depending on how they are treated, one thing I would recommend is taking away the aggravated damage lash, easy agg to everything is something Chronicles chose to avoid most of its lifespan. <br /> <br /> For antagonists you need something strong enough to be a massive threat, the God Machine, Conspiracies, Judges, and Exarchs are great options but I don't think it has to go that high if you, a rank 6+ epheral entity is plenty strong to force everyone to come together, but so is an elder vampire or a particularly powerful Mummy or Mage. Heck, you could even do a more exotic threat like a Pangean. You probably want at least 2 as was mentioned above but I think 3 is better, a third antagonist faction brings a lot of depth and options, but I think more than that can get too muddy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T12:18:19-07:00","id":1524602,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised no one brought up The Contagion Chronicle yet, so here's me advising you check that and the Player Guide for good directions. Beast is controversial, but it's storytelling chapter and Crossover discussion in Chapter 5 is also useful.<br /> <br /> You can come up with just about any argument that you want for how the group gets together-while each splat's metaphysics usually does a lot to immerse them in their corner of reality, monsters of various sorts do collide and run into each other reasonably a fair amount, and those bumps and stumbles can lead to odd friendships and communal goals-but it's worth noting that the reason your player characters get together is gonna set a lot of the tone for the chronicle. A group of monsters who gathered in the same apartment because they didn't run into anyone else from their corner and just rely and trust in each other is gonna be out for a different Chronicle set from a group of monsters on a military drive to kill God(whatever they think that is).<br /> <br /> As for what to include, it again depends on what the overarching goal and gameplay style for the game is going to be, but a good thing to keep in mind for designing opposition is that you need scaled opposition that plays into the strengths of the characters. I primarily bring this up because it can be intimidating to bring in the Arisen, the Awakened, and the Unchained into a crossover game, (and depending on your players, you might not have to), but by giving them issues and opponents that can really hamper everyone else if they're not on the ball with it, you can allow them to act like giant trees in rainstorms for their group, handling issues that they feel rewarded for wrestling with while creating a space for smaller scaled players and opposition to work. Put another way, if you imagine everyone else as chess pieces, Mummies, mages, and demons work to make sure the board doesn't swallow them or change on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-27-2023, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T15:29:12-07:00","id":1524607,"title":"","content":"First of all, I wanted to thank everyone for their comments and send an update on what's in the plans so far:<br /> <br /> As for the characters, no one has decided yet, so there's nothing new that I can report, and it looks like there's a possible eighth player (OMG). As for where the chronicle will take place, it will be in a fictional city, a metropolis, but he intends to expand as the story progresses and as for the style, I don't really know how to say it in English, but I think it will be a more cinematographic style with peaks of action. This means that there will be serious moments with a possible micro-investigation and not much drama, but there will be &quot;frequent&quot; moments of action that can go from zero to 100 quickly. As for the theme... I think it's a bit of a war in the shadows, various groups ranging from conspiracies and cults to street gangs fighting over territories or hunting zones, for now he thought of a first antagonist that would be an attack group set up by a private company that detains and captures monsters to use in experiments (the worst part about this idea is that I liked it), but that's what we have so far. Also, can anyone give a tip on using mummy as a rival?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T16:27:05-07:00","id":1524608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524607#post1524607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, can anyone give a tip on using mummy as a rival?</div> </div> </div> </div>As an antagonist that eventually needs to be beaten sort of rival, or as a sometimes pain in the ass, sometimes ally sort of rival?<br /> <br /> In either case, a mummy (be they Arisen, Deceived, or Shuankhsen) are pretty good mid-chronicle twists for a narrative, and generally for a narrative on the whole with early bits of a chronicle conflicting against a mummy's cult, which is already a good opportunity to introduce unique antagonists and future supportive characters between sorcerers, relic-wielding specialists, ghosts and spirits(Particularly if you keep some of the kickstarter text on Utterances that kept more of an eye on spirits), Imbued individuals, Deviants, and the odd other splat to come in-the Judge(/temakh/Ammut) and Guild of the mummy in question gives you a direction and way to understand they're interacting with the chronicle without outright defining what they're about, and that variety makes for a great excuse to have a diverse, stand out cast of antagonists who can change over the game.<br /> <br /> The middle of a chronicle becomes a great time to then summon the said Mummy, because the height of the mummy's power lets them radically change the nature of the game with their farther reaching powers, and their individual power can lead to a lot of tense conflict-a mummy awakening is great fodder for a Knight of Cerebus moment, and can become a wrecking ball to any complacency or reliance in the setting and developing narrative, and that in turn can incentivize the other major players of the setting to accelerate their projects or shift goals. By this point, you can reasonably figure out what the mummy's and cult's goals and main modus operandi are, so you can firm up all the details you left lying around into a direction you need to to make the game what you need it to be. And, of course, you don't need to worry too much about what happens if they knock out the mummy (or their Sadikh/Fasad, if you're employing one). Awakening a mummy is, in short, just a great time to really start the climax and to make a memorable shift in the story, the sort of thing players are likely to be talking about for years.<br /> <br /> And in the close of the game, the Mummy's waning power and increased interest in Memory allows for you get a catharsis in a wide variety of ways. If you want to go with a pure antagonist, the cult's weariness from running this entire time is likely in place, they are a lot easier to put down, if not in a position to go down for an extended, taken out of the chronicle death cycle, and the increase in Memory also means that your players have more avenues to get at them. All of those factors also lead well into diplomatic or change of heart sort of answers as well, too, and in a game that's leading up to it's final conflict, getting the long experience and occult knowledge (and even occult power, just because they can't destroy a city anymore doesn't mean that low tier Utterances and Affinities aren't potent tools all the same) can be a massive boon against final antagonists.<br /> <br /> Mummies, of all the varieties, make for good rivals primarily because they have so many ways they can come and get into the fray, and the nature of working through cults and the way Memory can change the game means they have a lot of versatility in how they can complicate or drive conflicts. Their Power is always a great way to shock the game, and whether you introduce it in the middle, beginning, or end, it's bound to be a really rewarding way to set the story.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with them, and the reason why I opt for mid-chronicle, is that it <i>can</i> be easy for a Mummy to be overwhelming-you want to pay attention to what the cast of player characters have and make sure you don't build your mummy in such a way that they can't escape it and live to fight it another day. That's true of any antagonist you design to come up multiple times in a game, but because mummies do start off with an assumption of power that is reasonably part of the reason you'd want to use them for, you want to be particularly careful on that. By the middle of a chronicle, the PC's should be empowered enough to have plenty of answers, and certainly by the end of a Chronicle that'll be the case, so you don't have to worry about it, but if you start the chronicle with a mummy awakening and doing their shit, it pays to give that attention.<br /> <br /> Anything more might need more details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T19:36:12-07:00","id":1524611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524608#post1524608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an antagonist that eventually needs to be beaten sort of rival, or as a sometimes pain in the ass, sometimes ally sort of rival?<br /> <br /> In either case, a mummy (be they Arisen, Deceived, or Shuankhsen) are pretty good mid-chronicle twists for a narrative, and generally for a narrative on the whole with early bits of a chronicle conflicting against a mummy's cult, which is already a good opportunity to introduce unique antagonists and future supportive characters between sorcerers, relic-wielding specialists, ghosts and spirits(Particularly if you keep some of the kickstarter text on Utterances that kept more of an eye on spirits), Imbued individuals, Deviants, and the odd other splat to come in-the Judge(/temakh/Ammut) and Guild of the mummy in question gives you a direction and way to understand they're interacting with the chronicle without outright defining what they're about, and that variety makes for a great excuse to have a diverse, stand out cast of antagonists who can change over the game.<br /> <br /> The middle of a chronicle becomes a great time to then summon the said Mummy, because the height of the mummy's power lets them radically change the nature of the game with their farther reaching powers, and their individual power can lead to a lot of tense conflict-a mummy awakening is great fodder for a Knight of Cerebus moment, and can become a wrecking ball to any complacency or reliance in the setting and developing narrative, and that in turn can incentivize the other major players of the setting to accelerate their projects or shift goals. By this point, you can reasonably figure out what the mummy's and cult's goals and main modus operandi are, so you can firm up all the details you left lying around into a direction you need to to make the game what you need it to be. And, of course, you don't need to worry too much about what happens if they knock out the mummy (or their Sadikh/Fasad, if you're employing one). Awakening a mummy is, in short, just a great time to really start the climax and to make a memorable shift in the story, the sort of thing players are likely to be talking about for years.<br /> <br /> And in the close of the game, the Mummy's waning power and increased interest in Memory allows for you get a catharsis in a wide variety of ways. If you want to go with a pure antagonist, the cult's weariness from running this entire time is likely in place, they are a lot easier to put down, if not in a position to go down for an extended, taken out of the chronicle death cycle, and the increase in Memory also means that your players have more avenues to get at them. All of those factors also lead well into diplomatic or change of heart sort of answers as well, too, and in a game that's leading up to it's final conflict, getting the long experience and occult knowledge (and even occult power, just because they can't destroy a city anymore doesn't mean that low tier Utterances and Affinities aren't potent tools all the same) can be a massive boon against final antagonists.<br /> <br /> Mummies, of all the varieties, make for good rivals primarily because they have so many ways they can come and get into the fray, and the nature of working through cults and the way Memory can change the game means they have a lot of versatility in how they can complicate or drive conflicts. Their Power is always a great way to shock the game, and whether you introduce it in the middle, beginning, or end, it's bound to be a really rewarding way to set the story.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with them, and the reason why I opt for mid-chronicle, is that it <i>can</i> be easy for a Mummy to be overwhelming-you want to pay attention to what the cast of player characters have and make sure you don't build your mummy in such a way that they can't escape it and live to fight it another day. That's true of any antagonist you design to come up multiple times in a game, but because mummies do start off with an assumption of power that is reasonably part of the reason you'd want to use them for, you want to be particularly careful on that. By the middle of a chronicle, the PC's should be empowered enough to have plenty of answers, and certainly by the end of a Chronicle that'll be the case, so you don't have to worry about it, but if you start the chronicle with a mummy awakening and doing their shit, it pays to give that attention.<br /> <br /> Anything more might need more details.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they are aware for the most part, if possible I wanted examples of how the mummy would operate considering she might even have to cooperate with other monsters or compete against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T12:01:29-07:00","id":1524698,"title":"","content":"Something that no-one seems to have brought up yet is just how all of these Supernatural Beings came together as a group. True, in some cases certain players <i>could</i> be relatively easy 'package orders', such as any Ghouls present being the thralls of any PC Vampires, or Wolf-Blooded being connected to any of the available Urathra by being part of the same bloodline, or a Hero being connected to one of the Troupe's Begotten, but the gamelines rarely have much interest in looking for each other, at least beyond those Beasts who're seeking out non-mortal, non-Horror (the random gribblies type, not the Beast-Soul-Equivalent variety) Kin, or individuals seeking to understand other supernatural 'races'.<br /> <br /> Maybe they each stumbled across some sort of thread that piqued their interest, started following it, ran into each other &amp; somehow realised or uncovered that all their seemingly disparate &amp; disconnected lines of inquiry were actually\u200b connected, or at least sufficiently close in relation that it be more advantageous/convenient to work together than alone, somehow? Also, are they sticking with JUST the Canon gamelines, or are they adding in fan-made ones like Princess, Genius, Leviathan, Hunchback, Psychic, Dragon (be it Inheritance or Embers), Alien: The Stranded, Monarch: the Endless, etc., etc.?<br /> <br /> Also, that group your guy mentioned sounds similar to the Cheiron Group from H:tV... I think, I've admittedly not had much of a chance to read up on either the 'Big Three' or Hunter yet. Do they have any particular drive behind their capturing of, &amp; experimentation upon, monsters? As in, are they trying to understand the supernaturals, control them, make some sort of profit off of them somehow, just because they can, or something different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 10-29-2023, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T13:49:40-07:00","id":1524713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524698#post1524698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that no-one seems to have brought up yet is just how all of these Supernatural Beings came together as a group. True, in some cases certain players <i>could</i> be relatively easy 'package orders', such as any Ghouls present being the thralls of any PC Vampires, or Wolf-Blooded being connected to any of the available Urathra by being part of the same bloodline, or a Hero being connected to one of the Troupe's Begotten, but the gamelines rarely have much interest in looking for each other, at least beyond those Beasts who're seeking out non-mortal, non-Horror (the random gribblies type, not the Beast-Soul-Equivalent variety) Kin, or individuals seeking to understand other supernatural 'races'.<br /> <br /> Maybe they each stumbled across some sort of thread that piqued their interest, started following it, ran into each other &amp; somehow realised or uncovered that all their seemingly disparate &amp; disconnected lines of inquiry were actually\u200b connected, or at least sufficiently close in relation that it be more advantageous/convenient to work together than alone, somehow? Also, are they sticking with JUST the Canon gamelines, or are they adding in fan-made ones like Princess, Genius, Leviathan, Hunchback, Psychic, Dragon (be it Inheritance or Embers), Alien: The Stranded, Monarch: the Endless, etc., etc.?<br /> <br /> Also, that group your guy mentioned sounds similar to the Cheiron Group from H:tV... I think, I've admittedly not had much of a chance to read up on either the 'Big Three' or Hunter yet. Do they have any particular drive behind their capturing of, &amp; experimentation upon, monsters? As in, are they trying to understand the supernaturals, control them, make some sort of profit off of them somehow, just because they can, or something different?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the ST already has an idea similar to this to bring the group together, but he prefers not to resort to it, as it is a resource that he considers forced, so he is using up his options before use this. Secondly, fan-made games, as far as I know, haven't become popular in my country, I myself have only heard about Princess and Alien, so no, he won't use. Third, look... I'm not 100% sure of the objective, at first it seems just for personal gain, but who knows what he will do with it later? Besides this group want to use supernaturals for personal gain, control them to use as shock troops, research your abilities in order to replicate them, the basic, in this conversation I even suggested a procedure for making a Synthetic Dalu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T16:17:25-07:00","id":1524777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524608#post1524608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything more might need more details.</div> </div> </div> </div>What could you tell me about a mummy vs. mummy situation? One of the players is thinking about using an Arisen character so it would be useful to have one or two antagonists linked to him, if helps, his judge seems to be that of the death of several people, to not to use another term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T12:06:22-07:00","id":1524825,"title":"","content":"The last game i ran i required one thing of my players (during character creation they all had to be anti-war) and then I let them come up with any background they wanted to explain why they were anti-war (though one ended up as an arms dealer) it worked because this one thing in common brought the characters together, but they had control over the details...<br /> <br /> Basically you can railroad in a good way, by putting all the characters together and then having the players justify how they got there running scene in flashback (so they players still have a lot of agency... And it is more of a collaborative storytelling approach).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T04:14:51-07:00","id":1524904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524713#post1524713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the ST already has an idea similar to this to bring the group together, but he prefers not to resort to it, as it is a resource that he considers forced, so he is using up his options before use this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, apologies then. It was the first thing that came to mind, &amp; I figured that I'd at least try to contribute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524713#post1524713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, fan-made games, as far as I know, haven't become popular in my country, I myself have only heard about Princess and Alien, so no, he won't use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty then, at least that helps narrow things down by a lot, which should make attempts to help easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524713#post1524713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, look... I'm not 100% sure of the objective, at first it seems just for personal gain, but who knows what he will do with it later? Besides this group want to use supernaturals for personal gain, control them to use as shock troops, research your abilities in order to replicate them, the basic, in this conversation I even suggested a procedure for making a Synthetic Dalu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... So mostly just your average, 'generic', greedy, Immoral (or at least <i>A</i>moral), money-obsessed, power-hungry (Mega?)Corporation. Nothing wrong with that, was just vaguely interested in whether or not he was attempting to spice things up a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T19:10:12-07:00","id":1524953,"title":"","content":"These are some groups/factions that I thought of for the chronicle in question, they are just the thoughts of a Brainstorm so forgive me for the simplicity, I would like a second opinion to make sure that no idea was too incoherent and if anyone has any ideas too I am grateful.<br /> <br /> Private company: Basically the same idea that I mentioned at the beginning of a private company that captures and studies supernaturals to use, study and (possibly) replicate their abilities, however I decided to expand this idea a little; while part of the company, the most mundane part, only thinks about the profit of the venture, the real bosses would be other supernaturals who have other objectives, among the options I thought:<br /> <br /> - The owner of the company is actually a kindred, or a group of them, who hope through research to find a way to get rid of their weaknesses, such as their curse or even vulnerability to the sun, if this is not possible, they could still use them as tools against their enemies;<br /> <br /> - The company would be a tool of the God Machine that intends to use other monsters to exert its control or sees them as anomalies that must be neutralized. My doubt about this scenario is that I don't really know how GM reasons, so I don't know if this would be a typical attitude of the system. In the second case, I could alternatively use an angel or fallen one who is acting independently and uses this group to study (or erase) other monsters as he believes they are GM creations or errors;<br /> <br /> - This one is quite forced, but it can be used, the owner of the company could be someone who saw the future (an arisen or a mage) and is doing everything to prevent some terrible event from happening, like a possible apocalypse, so he founded the company and looks to the supernatural for any way to acquire power, alternatively he could just be a madman who believes he has seen the future, but is just delusional. I know this is really weird, but I needed to comment.<br /> <br /> Carthano Family (Don't even ask where I got this name): Basically it's a mafia family that uses the undead and ghosts in their business, basically the Giovanni from WOD, but with much less detail. In this case, a large part of the group would be made up of Ghost Eaters and necromancers. They would be a minor faction and just an occasional headache, nothing too complicated and could be used as a hook for the Sin-eaters if someone wants a character like that. Now if they were to have a more impactful role, I thought the head of the family could be a vampire, a arisen, some kind of immortal, basically someone very old who has been in this business for a long time and uses someone as a puppet to command the operations without him needing to show himself publicly, or in sunlight in the case of the vampire.<br /> <br /> Beast Corp's: It's a provisional name, basically it's a group of devoured that operate with other factions or privately and use their skills in exchange for money and favors, but that's just superficially, internally this group is a Tyrany, every devoured in the city ends up being forced to join, once inside the group they get money and to a certain extent guaranteed 'food', as long as they follow the rules. The leader of the group is an incarnate beast who strongly believes that the Dark Mother's children are superior creatures to other monsters and that they eventually will be at the top of the food chain, he goes so far as to massacre any group that is forming, especially changelings, believing that they are the most vulnerable, or Promethians, as he finds them shameful, but he does not attack larger or already well-established groups, as he knows that shouldn't be starting fights with everyone. It is also because of this group that heroes aren't a problem in the city, they quickly are killed.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T04:17:46-07:00","id":1525018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524953#post1524953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are some groups/factions that I thought of for the chronicle in question, they are just the thoughts of a Brainstorm so forgive me for the simplicity, I would like a second opinion to make sure that no idea was too incoherent and if anyone has any ideas too I am grateful.<br /> <br /> Private company: Basically the same idea that I mentioned at the beginning of a private company that captures and studies supernaturals to use, study and (possibly) replicate their abilities, however I decided to expand this idea a little; while part of the company, the most mundane part, only thinks about the profit of the venture, the real bosses would be other supernaturals who have other objectives, among the options I thought:<br /> <br /> - The owner of the company is actually a kindred, or a group of them, who hope through research to find a way to get rid of their weaknesses, such as their curse or even vulnerability to the sun, if this is not possible, they could still use them as tools against their enemies;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the Ordo Dracul's stick.<br /> <br /> Using scientific experimentation to discover new ways to avoid the curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The company would be a tool of the God Machine that intends to use other monsters to exert its control or sees them as anomalies that must be neutralized. My doubt about this scenario is that I don't really know how GM reasons, so I don't know if this would be a typical attitude of the system. In the second case, I could alternatively use an angel or fallen one who is acting independently and uses this group to study (or erase) other monsters as he believes they are GM creations or errors;\u200b </div> </div> </div>GM cults do exist afaik, but what exactly their purpose is depends on the inscrutible desires of the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> They are usually being used for a specific goal, as part of some infrastructure, or to achieve some goal. I'm not sure, I would have to re-read some...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T02:07:37-08:00","id":1525057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1524953#post1524953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The company would be a tool of the God Machine that intends to use other monsters to exert its control or sees them as anomalies that must be neutralized. My doubt about this scenario is that I don't really know how GM reasons, so I don't know if this would be a typical attitude of the system. In the second case, I could alternatively use an angel or fallen one who is acting independently and uses this group to study (or erase) other monsters as he believes they are GM creations or errors;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1525018#post1525018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GM cults do exist afaik, but what exactly their purpose is depends on the inscrutible desires of the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> They are usually being used for a specific goal, as part of some infrastructure, or to achieve some goal. I'm not sure, I would have to re-read some...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya' know, putting these two together <i>would</i> make sense, both narratively <i>&amp;</i> lore-wise. As in, the cult would believe that their deity wished to somehow deal with the 'Uncontrolled Variables' that were the various Splats, be it through thorough elimination, harvesting them for specific resources, turning them into '<i>Controlled</i> Variables,' or something else along those lines, and wanted its mortal followers to study the workings of such creatures so that they could better aid in erasing, harvesting, manipulating, or even outright controlling the supernatural entities they found. The details would still be ultimately up to the ST, obviously, but it's interesting to think on where the G-M could take this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T16:44:15-08:00","id":1525095,"title":"","content":"Here's an update on those who have already chosen characters.<br /> Two chose werewolves, cousins apparently, the characters, not the players;<br /> An Arisen;<br /> And a curious thing, a character who was once a mage, but was remade and became a cyborg, I think, I didn't quite understand, and he also has amnesia.<br /> <br /> Now, how did they meet? This isn't even me asking for advice, I'm just curious how you would fit this together.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T19:25:49-08:00","id":1525104,"title":"","content":"All three of those monster-types are very goal-driven, so in theory it'd be as simple as them being headed in the same direction for compatible reasons, e.g. the mummy is after a relic being used by one of the deviant's Conviction Touchstones to control/summon/empower a monster that the werewolves are hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T07:01:58-08:00","id":1525116,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of ways to do it, and a large part of that depends on how you want your players to feel. <br /> <br /> Big Damn Heroes: I think tying the Deviant's conspiracy to the Uratha's enemies is an easy way to tie those two together. For the mummy I would probably have the Judge's be interested in what the conspiracy was doing and the Mummy PC is supposed to stop them, but perhaps avoid killing certain, key individuals. <br /> <br /> Little Fish: An alternate way of doing it is have the PCs all in one specific location when something big and bad happens and they get caught up in it. Over time they gradually get to realize they were all manipulated into being at the location by either a person, an organization, or even the God Machine and they're all just puppets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T07:51:44-08:00","id":1525456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1525095#post1525095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a curious thing, a character who was once a mage, but was remade and became a cyborg, I think, I didn't quite understand, and he also has amnesia.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Please tell me he is an Extempore Promethean rather than a Deviant, because if so, you absolutely should consider getting a Sin-Eater in your group whose Geist is the result of the original Mage's Ghost.<br /> Lots of shenanigans to play with there, and a very natural reason to group them up: get the soul and body back together, maybe even look for ways to recombine them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Getting the Uratha and the Deviant Cyborg to group up? Other than what was mentioned, you could go with Awkward First Meeting: misunderstanding the Cyborg's nature, the Uratha start to hunt him as a Claimed, but the cyborg proves tough, smart and honorable, slowly earning their respect. Researching their prey and gradually uncovering what has happened to them, throw in some 3rd party involvement forcing them to cooperate or even be saved by the cyborg (likely unwittingly), and they started regretting their decision to hunt the cyborg, who they have come to like by now. To make up for almost murdering the Cyborg, they agree to help with the revenge - bonus points for Iron Master Uratha and a Conspiracy that meddles with Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T11:18:05-08:00","id":1525462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524568-cross-over-team?p=1525456#post1525456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please tell me he is an Extempore Promethean rather than a Deviant, because if so, you absolutely should consider getting a Sin-Eater in your group whose Geist is the result of the original Mage's Ghost.<br /> Lots of shenanigans to play with there, and a very natural reason to group them up: get the soul and body back together, maybe even look for ways to recombine them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting their ghost to transform into a gesit seems like it should take a while, whereas you can create a ghost without dying (doppleganger), especially if you experience a serious life changing experience (the death of the old part of their life).<br /> <br /> And a ghost can be playable on its own, any other character aware of ghosts could notice it hanging around (using their body as an anchor... That is normal if the body is dead, does it still apply for dopplegangers?) And with the Amnesia, the dopplegangers might be the only entity which has access to their older memories (not that the players might be aware of such).<br /> <br /> Turning them into a geist without first losing all their anchors seems odd, but I guess the Promethean might be fairly distant (in time) from the ghost's creation..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T18:02:10-08:00","id":1525489,"title":"","content":"I don't believe Geists necessarily have to lose their anchors in second edition, they just have to survive drinking from one of the underworld rivers and while it does imply a significant amount of banked XP it isn't, strictly speaking, required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T15:51:01-08:00","id":1525546,"title":"","content":"Okay, the final group looked like this: Two Uratha, two Beasts, a mummy, a sin-eater, and a deviant who was once a mage. As for what makes everyone form a gang (?), for that I'll need to explain a little about the state of the city and let me warn you that I didn't fully understand ST's intention with this, so I'm sorry if there is any inconsistency.<br /> <br /> In the city in question where the chronicle takes place there is an abnormally high number of supernatural creatures, but those who establish the greatest control are the kindred who control most of the high positions in gorvement and in high places, followed by the werewolves who have a good portion of the city From what I understand there were several packs and they operated almost like gangs. This all changed when a local company, Biovolt, was acquired by an anonymous buyer and it sundenly became interested in the supernatural. Both Kindred and Uratha soon noticed this and each decided to prepare their own countermeasures, but Biovolt was faster and carried out a series of successful surprise attacks, on shelters and meeting places, all in the space of two or three days. A faction of beasts was formed due to what happened and occupied a good part of the other groups' former hunting areas. This situation was only so favorable to their interests because they managed to make an agreement with Biovolt quietly.<br /> The end result of these attacks was that the werewolves lost many of their number and were forced into hiding and many of the survivors are now wanted criminals, but not all of then. As for the kindred, they practically disappeared from sight, many of their hiding places were discovered, minions killed or captured, but the truth is that some remain in the city just waiting for the dust to settle or looking for a chance to escape.<br /> <br /> Returning to the pack, the two uratha belonged to one of the packs that were attacked by Biovolt, in their case, their pack was called for a meeting from another packs, as they arrived late for reasons not yet specified, they arrived after end of the attack, so they avoided the worst, but they weren't going to last long without the protection of a pack, without others of their species they could turn to. They got in touch with Castro, the Arisen.<br /> <br /> Castro had some followers working at Biovolt, but they disappeared after its acquisition, this was around the time he awakened again in this era, he suspects it was the work of another Arisen, as the purchase of the company doesn't fit with his memories and so he decides to investigate, but he cannot count on his minions for certain tasks and even he would have problems alone considering the kind of firepower that Biovolt has at its disposal now, so he sought help from unlikely places, with the Uratha and in exchange for temporary shelter he wants their help and that of others.<br /> <br /> Jack, the sin-eater, is a nomad, but he came to the city after his aunt Nonna who was also a sin-eater and part of a krewe, but when he arrives, everyone disappears and whatall suggests is that they were captured and the pack of two Stooges had a protection agreement with the krewe that they seem to have ignored for reasons they refuse to talk about and now Jack is demanding their help and that's why he joined the party and also because he needs a place to stay and Castro has money. An extra detail Nonna and the uratha's pack leader were lovers. I know nothing about the ghost.<br /> <br /> Now the beasts, one of them is a ghoul from a kindred who needs to isolate himself and the beast is now his eyes and ears in the city and also the one who brings him food. The other is called Bea and joins the group allegedly for protection, but in reality she is being intimidated by the beast faction to spy on Castro, and she is also the ex-gf of one of the uratha.<br /> <br /> The deviant was once a mage, but he was transformed and he doesn't know how because he lost his memory of the last two weeks and woke up inside a luxury hotel with a man in a coma next to him and all this in the middle of a shootout that practically destroyed an entire floor (Yeah, this is crazy). He ran away and ended up bumping into the group, they didn't explain to me how, but Castro decided to take him in as he could be a clue about what was happening inside Biovolt. Some more details are that he was suspected of having participated in the hotel shooting; The ghouled beast already knows him from a meeting that he had with his master during the period of amnesia, but he keeps it a secret and the man in a coma in the hotel room was part of Nonna's krewe, meaning it's a very delicate situation.<br /> <br /> This is how the group ended up, it seems like a decent prelude or the beginning of a parody of a Mexican soap opera and a generic South American gang film, usually Colombian for some reason.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T16:33:07-08:00","id":1525757,"title":"","content":"I know I\u2019m late to the party but the Contagion Chronicle book might help. It lists various organizations that notice distortions in reality and whatnot. This sounds cheesy but the players could just get a call to show up at a diner, then the \u201cI know this seems random, but we need a squad of special people for a special task\u201d kinda thing. Or \u201cuniqueness in your fields\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}